<node id="1218618" title="Re^2: IF condition with a range (updated)" created="2018-07-16 19:54:44" updated="2018-07-16 19:54:44" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="524150">syphilis</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;I&gt;if (abs($y-$x) &lt;= 1)&lt;/I&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
It's perhaps worth noting that, with floats, if &lt;c&gt;$x == $y&lt;/c&gt; it does not necessarily follow that &lt;c&gt;$x - $y == 0&lt;/c&gt;, or that &lt;c&gt;abs($x - $y) &lt;= 1&lt;/c&gt;
&lt;br&gt;If $x and $y are both infinities (of the same sign) then the first condition holds true, while the second and third are false.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cheers,&lt;br&gt;Rob</doctext>
